## Multi-Browser Automation Control System

### Overview

A complete Playwright-based E2E testing framework for the SwimChain forum-client with **multi-instance browser control** - meaning you can run multiple browser instances simultaneously for testing scenarios like:

- User A sponsors User B (two browsers interacting)
- Concurrent thread viewing
- Race condition testing

### Architecture

```
forum-client/tests/e2e/
├── browser/
│   └── BrowserManager.ts      # Multi-instance browser orchestration
├── pages/                     # Page Object Model
│   ├── BasePage.ts            # Common page utilities
│   ├── LoginPage.ts           # Identity/login flows
│   ├── SpaceListPage.ts       # Space navigation
│   ├── ThreadPage.ts          # Thread interactions
│   └── SponsorshipPage.ts     # Sponsorship offer flows
├── helpers/
│   ├── navigation.ts          # URL routing, wait utilities
│   └── forum.ts               # Forum-specific actions
├── core/
│   └── TestRunner.ts          # Test orchestration engine
├── multi-instance-example.spec.ts  # Example test
└── playwright.config.ts       # Configuration
```

### Key Components

**1. BrowserManager** (`browser/BrowserManager.ts`)

Manages multiple browser instances with named access:

```typescript
const manager = new BrowserManager();
await manager.launch('alice');
await manager.launch('bob');

const alicePage = manager.getPage('alice');
const bobPage = manager.getPage('bob');

// Alice and Bob can interact simultaneously
await alicePage.goto('/spaces');
await bobPage.goto('/sponsorships');

await manager.closeAll();
```

**2. Page Objects** (`pages/`)

Each page has a dedicated class encapsulating selectors and actions:

```typescript
// LoginPage
await loginPage.enterIdentity(keypair);
await loginPage.submit();

// SpaceListPage  
await spaceListPage.navigateToSpace('test-space');

// ThreadPage
await threadPage.createPost('Hello world');
await threadPage.replyTo(postId, 'Nice post!');

// SponsorshipPage
await sponsorshipPage.claimOffer(offerId);
await sponsorshipPage.fillClaimForm({ wallet: '...' });
```

**3. Navigation Helpers** (`helpers/navigation.ts`)

```typescript
await navigateTo(page, '/spaces/abc123');
await waitForPage(page, 'space-view');
await clickAndWait(page, 'button.submit', 'success-toast');
await fillForm(page, {
  '#name': 'Alice',
  '#bio': 'SwimChain enthusiast'
});
```

**4. Forum Helpers** (`helpers/forum.ts`)

SwimChain-specific utilities:

```typescript
await createTestIdentity();
await postToSpace(page, spaceId, 'Test message');
await engageWithContent(page, contentId);
await waitForDecay(page, contentId);
```

**5. TestRunner** (`core/TestRunner.ts`)

Orchestrates complex multi-step test scenarios:

```typescript
const runner = new TestRunner();
runner.addStep('setup', async () => { ... });
runner.addStep('action', async () => { ... });
runner.addStep('verify', async () => { ... });
await runner.run();
```

### Example Test

```typescript
// multi-instance-example.spec.ts
test('Alice sponsors Bob', async () => {
  const manager = new BrowserManager();

  // Launch two browsers
  await manager.launch('alice');
  await manager.launch('bob');

  const alicePage = new SponsorshipPage(manager.getPage('alice'));
  const bobPage = new SponsorshipPage(manager.getPage('bob'));

  // Bob creates an offer
  await bobPage.createOffer({ amount: 100, description: 'Need sponsor' });
  const offerId = await bobPage.getOfferId();

  // Alice claims it
  await alicePage.navigateToOffer(offerId);
  await alicePage.claimOffer();

  // Verify both sides see the update
  await expect(alicePage.getStatus()).resolves.toBe('claimed');
  await expect(bobPage.getStatus()).resolves.toBe('claimed');

  await manager.closeAll();
});
```

### How It Was Built

The ABUDDI orchestration decomposed the task:

| Agent | Responsibility |
|-------|----------------|
| **Product Maestro** | Scored 33/60, delegated to 3 Feature Owners |
| **Feature Owner 1** | Browser framework (BrowserManager, launch/close/getInstance) |
| **Feature Owner 2** | Test scenarios (example specs) |
| **Feature Owner 3** | Test orchestration (TestRunner, helpers) |
| **9 Sub-ICs** | Individual components (pages, helpers, config) |

Total: **13 agent contexts** working in parallel, each with fresh context windows.

